   156	**5. 2D tangent-sweep / pole-cancellation saturation** (row 34; Sol 7 and 6 — his best disproof experiment; Grok scores only the descent framing, at 2 — dissent noted).
   157	*Experiment (Sol's spec):* Write the lowest-degree plane tangent-sweep ansatz with one controlled pole, impose polynomiality and determinant one as divisibility equations, and compute the saturation. Either a survivor reveals a new 2D mechanism, or a short unit identity documents the two-dimensional no-go — valuable either way.
