./xmodel/grok-approaches.md:12:**The one campaign fact that must color every local-at-infinity entry.** `REDUCTION.md` is the honest dependency audit: there is **no theorem** sending an arbitrary planar Keller counterexample into a currently enumerated sheet-book, and **no proved upper bound on topological degree**. Any approach that only kills `td ≤ 14` configurations, or only the residue-A chart, is not a JC2 program. It is a necessary-condition mill. The campaign knows this on paper and then proceeds as if the mill were the theorem. That is the central self-deception to refuse.
