./xmodel/sol-jvdk.log:2540:./xmodel/sol-gluing.out:9833:xmodel/sol-avenues2.md:244:The residue-A identities provide a positive control: the two paths close at the exceptional ratio \(2\pm\sqrt3\). Exact-budget off-axis routes leave no hidden charged vertex to absorb a mismatch, and the Jacobian inhomogeneity (\(-42\) on sheet 6, \(-\kappa\) in a general chart) fixes the last global scale. Depth conservation is essential: without it the eliminant would merely restate a finite per-route computation.
