./xmodel/sol-symplectic.log:3443:xmodel/sol-jvdk.log:2480:./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:6536:3. **“The full JC2 program is finite at every level” confuses pointwise finiteness with termination.** Finiteness for each fixed \((m,td)\) gives infinitely many books; only \(td\le14\) was enumerated and the degree farm stops at 150. Moreover, killing residue-A would still leave four single-pole \(td=6\) classes, while the composite single-pole residual grows to 212 classes at \(td=16\). There is no uniform \(td\)-bound, induction, or stabilization theorem. Thus “one template away from JC2” is not justified.
