./xmodel/sol-symplectic.log:3445:xmodel/sol-jvdk.log:2482:./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:6566:   Test whether the formal \(42\)-conjugate Puiseux orbit satisfies any polynomial relation with the prescribed Newton support. First computation: at depth \(N=\#(\Delta_f\cap\mathbb Z^2)+20\), compute the monomial-evaluation matrix modulo two good primes on the saturated residue-A locus. Uniform full rank kills algebraization; a one-dimensional kernel reconstructs \(f\), after which \(J(f,g)=1\) is linear in the coefficients of \(g\).
./xmodel/sol-symplectic.log:3446:xmodel/sol-jvdk.log:2483:./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:6579:The program’s likeliest genuine breakthrough is a **global algebraization obstruction** for the residue-A template—effectivity, polar data, or coefficient transport at the resonant direction—not another vertex-local identity. The template has survived too many exact local, coefficient, and topological checks to expect an easy kill.
