./xmodel/sol-symplectic.log:4029:dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/grok-nfz-final.md:94:  **Policy for emptiness is still sound.** Rule 6: an open obligation may emit `OPEN` / a symbolic candidate; it may not certify an empty panel. Leaving SD-fail and multi-word entries on the fat record, and forbidding quotient-based emptiness there, is exactly that rule. The ordered-free-zone enrichment is the *right missing datum for prefix-δ* (an unbounded word over a finite residue alphabet). It does not by itself give a finite quotient, which is why fail-closed is required. That package is honest and is what the last review asked for on dagger.
