./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:3507:A first substantive issue is now clear: the sheet-frame bound `Σ κ_F(π_F−1) ≤ td−1` is a bound on critical-value vertices, not on the number of ramified points of the curve cover. The residue-A control itself has 42 simple ramification points at `td=6`, so interpreting the survey’s `N` as `td−1` would be false. I’m therefore structuring the computation parametrically—recording the minimum Hurwitz support each primitive group needs—and will only specialize to a cap where the repository actually justifies one.
