xmodel/grok-approaches.md-228-**(b) Not proved by the campaign; used as negative space.** Shaska arXiv:2607.20210v2: in dimension two, graded-equivariant Keller maps are automorphisms for *every* weight sign pattern. Homogeneous (ordinary \(\mathbb G_m\)) plane Keller maps being linear is classical and easy. Campaign cites this in `paper1/main.tex` and `RECON.md`. No independent graded search.
xmodel/grok-approaches.md-229-
xmodel/grok-approaches.md-230-**(c) Closed as a counterexample hunt, open as a hint.** There is no graded plane counterexample. A hypothetical JC2 counterexample has no \(\mathbb G_m\)-symmetry. That is consistent with GGV: the interesting polygons are *not* cones from the origin in a single weight. Searching for quasihomogeneous CEs is a dead disproof lane. As a proof lane, “reduce to the graded case” is false.
