xmodel/sol-approaches.md-32-## I. Direct algebra and geometry in the plane
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-33-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-34-### 1. Jung–van der Kulk / elementary degree descent
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-35-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-36-- **Essence.** Normalize a minimal Keller pair and imitate the affine/triangular reductions of a plane automorphism until one component degree drops.
--
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-276-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-277-### 35. Real-plane methods, Pinchuk phenomena, dynamics, and SOS/CAD
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-278-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-279-- **Essence.** Seek a real constant-Jacobian collision to disprove JC2, or use real foliations, half-Reeb components, positivity, and global inverse criteria to prove injectivity.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-280-- **Campaign:** **No.** Sparse rational SOS/Positivstellensatz was only proposed in [sol-lateral.md](sol-lateral.md); no real CAD or dynamical run was executed.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-281-- **Precise obstruction.** Pinchuk maps have nowhere-zero but nonconstant Jacobian, so they are not counterexamples. Complex collisions need not have real points, so real positivity cannot prove complex JC2. SOS over the real locus is almost orthogonal to emptiness of a complex coefficient variety and scales terribly.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-282-- **Cheapest experiment — 1/10 for proof, 3/10 for disproof reconnaissance.** Impose the simplest real-symmetric boundary ansatz, solve numerically for a collision, and exact-check any hit. Do not invest in global CAD unless a very small rigid ansatz first survives.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-283-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md:284:### 36. Symplectic/Lagrangian geometry and a two-dimensional tangent-sweep construction
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-285-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md:286:- **Essence.** Regard $\{P,Q\}=1$ as an exact algebraic symplectic map; for disproof, adapt the 2026 tangent-line sweep/polynomialization mechanism while canceling its ramification in only two coordinates.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-287-- **Campaign:** **No executed plane construction.** Related quotient/descent ideas occur only as proposals in [sol-lateral.md](sol-lateral.md) and literature reconnaissance in [RECON.md](../RECON.md).
xmodel/sol-approaches.md:288:- **Precise obstruction.** Noncompact symplectic local isomorphisms need not be proper, so symplecticity alone proves little. More concretely, the known sweep hides/polynomializes the bad divisor using a third coordinate; in two dimensions the ramification divisor has nowhere to go, and graded plane Keller maps are already automorphisms.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md:289:- **Cheapest experiment — 7/10.** Write the lowest-degree plane tangent-sweep ansatz with one controlled pole, impose polynomiality and determinant one as divisibility equations, and compute the saturation. Either a survivor reveals a new mechanism or a short unit identity exposes the two-dimensional no-go.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-290-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-291-### 37. Restriction, quotient, or invariant-surface descent of the three-dimensional counterexample
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-292-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-293-- **Essence.** Find an invariant graph/surface, a one-LND quotient, or two target combinations on which the known $3$-fold Keller collision induces a plane Keller collision.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-294-- **Campaign:** **No execution; explicitly proposed.** The one-LND quotient is listed in [sol-lateral.md](sol-lateral.md). The campaign’s Witt work notes that the literal three-dimensional datum can lift mod $4$, but that is not a descent.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-295-- **Precise obstruction.** A constant $3\times3$ determinant gives no constant $2\times2$ minor after restriction or quotient. Natural quotients acquire a factor such as $\kappa L^2$, and arbitrary invariant surfaces destroy étaleness; a collision may disappear under the two target coordinates.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-296-- **Cheapest experiment — 6/10.** Compute all low-degree polynomial invariants/semi-invariants of the counterexample’s evident vector fields and test every rank-two target combination for a constant induced Jacobian on an invariant graph.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-297-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md:298:### 38. Rational constant-Jacobian maps and pole removal (Vitushkin-type)
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-299-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-300-- **Essence.** Begin with a noninjective rational étale plane map and remove its poles by birational shears or blowdowns without introducing a third coordinate.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-301-- **Campaign:** **No.** I found no rational-map construction or pole-cancellation solve in the repository.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md:302:- **Precise obstruction.** Clearing a pole changes the Jacobian or leaves base points; the simple Vitushkin covering shape is incompatible with known polynomial Keller geometry. Two dimensions offer no spare coordinate in which to absorb a denominator.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-303-- **Cheapest experiment — 6/10.** Classify one-pole rational maps with constant rational Jacobian up to triangular birational changes, then solve the exact divisibility conditions for polynomial output and a retained collision.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-304-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-305-### 39. Naive scaling/deformation to the linear part
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-306-
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-307-- **Essence.** Use $F_t=t^{-1}F(tx)$ to connect a Keller map to its invertible linear part and argue invertibility cannot change with $t$.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-308-- **Campaign:** **No—and it should not be pursued in this form.** No such proof appears in the corpus.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-309-- **Precise obstruction.** Properness is not uniform in $t$; sheets can enter from or escape to infinity. The dimension-three counterexample deforms to its linear part, directly falsifying the naive deformation principle.
xmodel/sol-approaches.md-310-- **Cheapest experiment — 1/10.** None beyond documenting the escape divisor in the known counterexample. A viable deformation program would first need a new invariant controlling infinity uniformly, which makes it a different route.
